bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:79:* ''An admit carries across a seal roll only through its roll anchors.'' The gate reads the presented admit against the carriage board's counted revokes and the kapae antigen, and folds no allow roster (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/membership-doctrine">>).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:132:* ''Introduction and admission'': a user introduces; an operator admits; the answer consumes the introduction (operator ruling).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:134:* ''Kahu acts fall into four chartered classes'': ordinary (1-of-1); high-impact — charter, admission, trust root (3-of-5, or 2-of-3 for a small body); emergency (2-of-3, a narrow pre-authorized power reviewed by a later causal act); revocation (the threshold of the original act). A challenge appends to the record and may pause LOCAL reliance; it never halts the protocol. Admission of a Kahu or a Lamplighter always takes the seat quorum, and no ordinary single-seat class covers it; kapae and rolls take the quorum too; the user road rides its own bound (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/kahu#/seed-and-nexus">>).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:135:* ''Renewal runs as three sequences, kept apart'' (the realm feed, a per-renewal causal position, the KEL), and lapse arrives as three distinct events: signed departure, recorded removal by relation-scoped kapae, renewal supersession.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:151:* ''(c′) adopted.'' The HOST's gate reads and burns invites. The gate sorts every socket into same-operator · contracted · walker · stranger; under PRIVATE a stranger meets silence before any session frame. The guest carries its hosting grant; the hearth stores nothing about it. Invites mint by blind POPRF evaluation, so who-invited-whom stays non-computable. Revocation runs by kapae of the guest's leaf, by non-renewal, or by an epoch roll. Sybils meet tolerance, never detection.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:152:* ''The inviter's face never signs an invite'': that signature would link the inviter at redemption. The hearth's blind evaluation carries the proof instead.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:153:* ''V — vesting by class.'' A guest the HOST invites holds floor 1 at once; a guest a WALKER invites vests at the host's next roll. The roll reads as the household's consent to grow, and purpose labels separate the two classes without naming the minter. The built allowance carries the pre-answered dial of the user road's three; the operator's answer to a user's introduction stands owed, and until it lands a walker's token earns standing with no answer (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/membership-doctrine#/the-invite">>).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:165:* ''Guests'': the first ceremony runs with the host's own invites only. The hosted road builds whole before the ceremony (#/the-attractor): its doors stand built and stay shut on the day.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:168:* ''An operator's own herm'': an operator contracts their own herm with one signature, scoped to one place and one Nexus, and it falls with a kapae of the operator's admit.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:173:* ''No guardians on the day'': each face starts one-of-one on its own paper, and enrolment comes later by one typed first-enrolment event the face's own current key signs on its own log.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:176:* ''Per-Nexus identifiers'': an admit names a per-Nexus identifier, a random leaf no other Nexus can link. The face's lineage may re-issue it by a signed hand-over the gate verifies, and per-Nexus keys mint at random, never from the persona seed.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:177:* ''Every boot rests at the floor until a human unlocks'' (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/waking-floor">>). At the floor every fleet lane stays shut, and the custody write door, the rest door and the dyad door answer the daemon island alone. A bounded ember stays design input: it raises to SERVING alone, never signs or admits, runs on a count and never a clock, needs the device's own unlock plus a second signal, records each raise, and any other device of the human removes it.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:184:* ''Removal's reach'': four edges take a marker (dyad, vouch, member, carriage). A vouch edge answers to its voucher and to a chartered quorum; a seal roll carries every shadow; a standing shadow reaches every gate and drives a key roll; a contested tie keeps the shadow up; mutual removal ends in an explicit fork (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae#/four-edges">>).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:185:* ''The PersonaGroup stands as a Keyhive group'', so a seat's revocation rolls the key of every bag the group reaches (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae#/keys">>; a fresh group stays owed, `K12` of #/the-loops).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:192:* ''A joined device reads the hearth's corpus and keeps its own.'' A joinee mounts the hearth's `@lararium` corpus read-only beside its own, and its writes stay in its own; the oracle plane (the hearth's catalog, daemon doc and faces' planes) never crosses (`device-admit.ts#admitCanonDocs`). Row `W21` carries the build.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:199:* ''Each browser tab asks for its own unlock.'' A tab that attaches to the shared holder opens the keystore by its own ask of the person; the holder carries no unlock between tabs. The reason reads off the session law: a session wears its own face, so each tab answers for its own opening (#/rulings, a session wears the face). The ask admits a tab to its face's open hive and derives no key: the holder keeps a face's keys while some session of that face stands unlocked, and the last to close locks it (operator, 2026-10-18; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/session-unlock-2026">> #/what-both-faces-hold). Row `B1` carries the build.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:204:* ''A cabal shares through the faces its members choose'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-18, on the Teshima Family Council story). Kalani founds a private family council; Leilani, already standing on the DreamNet with several faces, chooses which of them join it, and a face she keeps back never learns the council exists. The council's hive reads as a Keyhive group with no key of its own: its members act through their own faces' identities, so nothing stands above them, and a presentation reads valid against the current set without naming which member made it (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/identity-classes">> #/the-handle-chain). Any current member's face promotes into the council's canon; a graft takes the threshold; a face leaves by its own act, and another's removal rides `kapae` at the threshold or a fork that omits the captor (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm">> #/the-unswept-corner); members read the owner-set as faces, never as humans. A private council declares no heraldry and lives in its members' address books under pet-names (cabal-realm #/heraldry). Row `K16` carries the story as `K15`'s acceptance.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:205:* ''The asker seals'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-19, F6's custody fork). Once the browser holder owns the Repo and the daemon kernel, it routes each sealed write to the admitted tab whose session caused it, else to any admitted, unlocked tab of that write's face; with no awake admitted tab, the write waits, named `seal-awaits-session`, never silent and never decided by a clock. No key material leaves a tab, and each sealer holds the row-class key the occupied carrier's overwrite proof opens. A SharedWorker carries no promise to run while its tabs freeze, and no `MessagePort` event reports a peer's death (round one, 2026-10-19), so a seal that waits names its wait.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:208:* ''Custody and identity read by capability, never by host'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-19: //"I consider node and browser isomorphic-by-intent. Eventually, a browser-vessel somewhere may grow comparable capabilities to a node vessel, and this pattern cascades outwards to all future vessels."//). Three rules hold on every vessel, present and planned: a vessel meets each face through that face's atom alone, its veil signing every dial, join, enrolment, sibling channel and daemon proof made on that face's behalf, never one device-wide key; a vessel holds a place signer exactly while it stands a floor, for the floor's allowlisted duties, under the pre-rotated place KEL; and a faceless vessel reading another's floor proves nothing private, reading the public shelf under the floor card's pin. A node's daemon auth, device-key signer, sibling enrolment and group-secret opener read the one vessel seed today (`open-node-vessel.ts`), and a browser's do the same (`open-browser-vessel.ts`); each is a bond owed, carried by `K15`.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:211:* ''Each realm stands under one charter, a seed's or a Nexus's'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-18). A council that meets at one hearth stands under that hearth's seed charter, and its guests' chosen faces walk there with no Nexus founded; a council two hearths carry stands under the Nexus those two found fresh, since a Nexus names the operators' relationship (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae">> #/edge-hands). A guest sees every realm its worn face stands in.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:226:* ''The Offering Antigen scope'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-14). A signed Offering act carries a stable scope, the joint Nexus AID its signed inception mints, beside `sealEpochCid` as the authorizing epoch. The receiver resolves its own charter scope, verifies the act's epoch inside that scope's locally held lineage, checks the quorum at that exact epoch, and only then folds; an act whose scope differs stays as foreign evidence outside the `kapae` and `un_kapae` fold, and an incomplete lineage reads `unavailable`. The joint inception image commits to the offer fingerprint and to both founders' fresh cold successor commitments, and a successor commitment a vault already used refuses, so the AID names one founding statement and two foundings by one roster never alias. The reason: a neighbour's condemnation copied onto another board reads as testimony, never as that board's verdict. The ruling flips on a case where two foundings by one roster must read as one Nexus (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/offering-antigen-scope-decision-record">>).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:229:* ''Guardian enrolment's shape'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-14). Each face founds one-of-one with no guardians, and its log's verifier knows a typed first-enrolment event from the start: the face's own current key signs it, it commits the guardian set and threshold, and the face's prefix stays as it stands; every later change to the set takes the guardians' authority. The event shape and its verifier land before the fence, so an enrolment never re-founds a face. The reason: a face founded alone keeps its Handle's history when guardians join a year later, and no third hand holds standing over a one-of-one face. The ruling flips on an existing event kind that already permits that first, face-key-signed transition. Guardian count, request authentication, the veto, death and succession stay open (#/open).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:231:* ''A realm's quorum and its boards'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-14). Each realm stands under ONE Nexus, which the vessel's first act there names and its edge ledger keeps; every reader takes the realm's quorum roster off that Nexus's charter, never off its own primary one; and the realm's boards key on the realm's own id, so a removal's record stays among its parties. The reason: authority comes from the governing charter while the record addresses the relation it affects. The ruling flips on a realm-native charter model with its own seat creation, migration and conflict rule (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae#/edge-hands">>).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:232:* ''A restore after guardian enrolment'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-15). A face's own bundle restores after it enrols guardians, so long as the face's log still holds the set its own root enrolled by the typed first event and no later event moved it; a guardian rotation that moves the set cuts every earlier bundle off. The restored face stands provisional as the restore's key-history ruling holds. The reason: enrolling guardians must never silently kill a person's own backups, and the guardians' rotation, not the enrolment, cuts off a stolen bundle. The ruling flips on a provisional gate that cannot stop a restored face from signing an authority-changing act before a party confirms it (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/custody#/the-restore">>).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:235:* ''A roll waits on its prior anchor'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-15). A seal roll refuses by name while the prior roll stands with no anchor, so no Nexus stacks a roll over a step its readers cannot yet carry across a removal. The reason: an admit carries across a seal roll only through its roll anchors, and a roll laid over an anchorless one strands every admit between them.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:237:* ''The admit's gate pin'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-15). The admit carriage and fleet-join answer sign a validated full `GateBundlePin` for the hearth's sovereign sync route at the named Nexus, read by `readGateBundlePin`; its digest derives from that object. Dials index by (hearth, Nexus, route, tier). Floor routes receive their own full pins through an authenticated relation or a carried signed pin set; an announcement never authenticates its own first pin. The reason: a digest alone gives an offline dialer no trusted route or key. The ruling flips on an equally authenticated digest-to-full-pin carrier with an unambiguous route and offline first contact.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:239:* ''Sharing after the gate'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-15). The proven same-operator class establishes transport alone. The session's proven face and scoped document view decide each document. A place arm reaches infrastructure alone; a PersonaGroup grant admits a sibling vessel of the same face and grants no blanket document access. Two tabs on one laptop wearing different faces see different books. The reason: transport kinship grants no document readership. The ruling flips on a scoped-view proof that another key carries the same face with exactly the same facets.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:240:* ''A device set aside'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-15). Each vessel face-key certificate binds its face key to its certified device edge. Before sorting a presentation as same-operator, the gate consults the fleet edge's shadow for that device edge and refuses while the mapping or fold reads unreadable. The wire carries only the face-scoped key. A restart and two-face witness gate the cutover. The reason: removal of a device must cut every face it wore. The ruling flips on causal withdrawal of every affected face certificate proven to reach every gate with no gap.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:241:* ''The contract seam'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-15). N2, N4 and N5 stand handed back. Train W owns the admit-carriage hunk of `nexus-contract.ts` for the cutover, keeps N's anchor and prior-roll checks, and lands the contract, `device-admit.ts`, fleet answer, verifier and vectors as one signed-shape change. The reason: one signature shape must cross every producer and reader together. The ruling flips on a proven independent carriage boundary that preserves those checks and signed bytes.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:251:* ''Sync carries; verification decides'' (operator, 2026-10-20, approving the research at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/identity-invariants-2026">> and the controller's leans). A mutable CRDT carries identity claims and never decides them. Each face holds, on each device, a ''sealed identity anchor'' in its own custody (a D row): its PersonaGroup, its persona-KEL prefix, a commitment to its root, its device edge's digest, and a known frontier that never falls. Only founding, admission and the recovery rites (guardian rotation, bundle restore, root cards) write an anchor; sync never writes one. Founding and admission acts, device edges and lease advances travel as signed records in the face's `@persona` plane, a signed-entry log every reader verifies against the anchor and the KEL; two signed acts at one sequence surface as a fork, never a CRDT winner. The face planes hold verified projections. A device reads freely; an act that widens authority (admit, grant, re-key, seal to a reader) checks the sealed frontier and refuses a target that names a newer bound, its receipt naming the frontier it acted under. Transparency and witnesses for equivocation wait for their own row. Wave C carries the build inside `K15` step 6.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:256:* ''The edge frontier'' (operator, 2026-10-20, approving the controller's leans after the research at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/edge-frontier-2026">>). Nothing signed today lets a reader tell a device never set aside from a raise erased or withheld, so the house adds a signed ''edge frontier'' per board, its own domain-separated certificate type, the persona KEL resolving its signer's key. Every hand that can raise on a board signs its own stream's frontier (a fleet board's root; a realm board's charter quorum, with its holder where vouch edges raise), and a frontier commits its counted acts through its boundary as a content-addressed snapshot, its parent frontier, and its roster and epoch lineage. A raise shadows its target at once for every reader that sees it, and counts toward widening once its signer registers it into the next frontier. Sync always carries acts, frontiers and snapshots. A widening act (admit, grant, a content key sealed or re-sealed to a reader) reads its target against a frontier of every raising hand that extends any head the reader pinned and includes every raise it has seen; it acts as of that frontier, its receipt naming it, and waits as unknown where none qualifies. Every fleet and realm founds with a signed empty genesis frontier, and an admit bundle carries the current frontier and its snapshot. Until the row stands built, absence reads clear for sync and for widening alike, the gap named. Row `K17`.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:268:`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/membership-doctrine#/the-invite`. The decisions below constrain a slice
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:272:* ''The knock.'' A gate answers an upgrade only on a path derived from its own key (`gateKnock` via `knockSegment` in `packages/lararium-mesh/src/gate-bundle.ts`), so a dialer holding no pin draws no HTTP 101 — the WireGuard mac1 shape. The path still rides the upgrade in the clear on plain `ws`; full client-proves-first waits for Noise IK (R-WIRE).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:281:* ''The socket's handshake changes once.'' R-WIRE and the face proof build as ONE wire train: the signed admit, then the fleet-join door, then one socket cutover (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof">>). The tree between those steps reads no earlier shape; it stands as a build order, never a compatibility mode.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:283:* ''`vessel found` keeps a charterless road.'' The Stable founding act becomes the HEARTH's rite; a herm still founds as a place with no face, and a joiner still founds through an admit.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:285:* ''Guardian placement'' reads as advice the house names at enrolment, never a refusal. ''QR pairing'' shows a check string on both screens after the channel opens.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:318:* ''Canon direction the build owes'': canon crosses hearth → leaf; a leaf never writes the hearth's canon documents, and edits land in the working layer. The admitted leaf-side mount flag stops mount-path writes, while Repo sync carries those documents in both directions.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:330:* ''What stands sealed'': the custody root and the `identity-anchors` family: the keyhive archive, each face's own veil archive (`veil-archive-g<group digest>.bin` on the node, keyed by its PersonaGroup; the browser's `veil-archive-h<N>` row still keys by handle index until `K15` step 6), each face's anchors and the anchor roster. A founding seals them from its first write and hands out every keyhive Archive it stood before the provider leaves; the veil derives from the sealed custody root; a seat (`custody-seat.ts`) carries one holder per identity home, and each row reads whole or refuses by name, never empty. A creator that stands again restores from its Archive: cap events carry membership and never a creator's key agreement state. A stand mints one contact card and its Archive leaves after that mint, so the Archive lineage opens every prekey the identity ever presented. A browser vessel keeps the Archives its founding and its admit hand out in its keystore beside the device seed, in the clear, until browser custody wraps both (`browser-keyhive-archive.ts`).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:334:* ''The fleet-join family'': one face's root-signed answer carries its device edge, signed gate carriage, island reach, sealed address secret, vessel face-key certificates and add-a-face grants. A join lands through one checked door. `device-admit/v1` names the internal signed edge format, and `cabal-join` still names people and realm admission.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:337:* ''The walk records'': each hearth a vessel walks at keeps one HOT row sealed under the VK, named by a digest of that hearth's gate key (`packages/lararium-node/src/node-walk-store.ts`). A record holds bearer invites, the hearth's grant and one receipt per carried document (`{ cid: "blake3:<hex>", ref, key }`, whose `key` opens that document), so it counts as a secret row. The row rests in the storage home of the custody seat: the store takes no directory, so no caller files it beside a document store the vessel key never spans. Nothing at a hearth's path reads as no walk there; a row that stands and does not open, opens to another shape, or rests filed under another hearth's name refuses the read, the list and the update by name, and an update seals a whole record or nothing. Each change reads, decides and seals under one custody holder, so one invite leaves a wallet once. A floor composition reads no walk record and presents no walk; a fresh browser device stands at the floor under its `#floor=` card, and a joined face crosses under its root-signed pin. A key that locks under a live walk costs the walk one message, which it logs. `lares walk`, `walk take` and `walk invite` ride the custody door (`walk.state` · `walk.take` · `walk.invite`): a carried invite as a verb's argument, or an invite as a verb's outcome, would rest in the daemon's document in the clear.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:338:* ''The hosting rows'': a hearth's hosting state, each spend and its walkers' carriage rest as HOT rows sealed under the VK, in the storage home of the custody seat (`packages/lararium-node/src/hosting-store.ts`, `hosting-carry.ts`). The sealed writer writes a whole file and appends to none, so each spend lands as ONE row of its own, named by a digest of its nonce or marker: the row's presence IS the burn, and it reads, decides and seals under one custody holder. The spend row commits a redemption, and what rides ahead of it re-derives: the grant from the epoch, the leaf, the nonce and the claim, so a crash before the answer replays as `retry`; the operator's counts from the rows standing, by name. A roll's state row commits the roll, and the hosting doc re-derives from it: the next roll and each sovereign stand land an act the sealed state holds and the doc lacks (`landHostingActs`). The sweep of dead epochs' rows passes through the seat's removal door (`removeCustodyRow`), which removes only a row this vessel's key opens; a spend that sealed after a roll retired its epoch burns nothing live and leaves with the next sweep. Each carried value rests as one row whose name carries its address and its length, so a guest's bytes read off its rows and no counter stands beside them. One process serves a hearth's carriage (the standing vessel's own gate, under its store claim), and its contacts and deposits run in turn, so a quota reads the bytes the last deposit left and a reclaim never discards on a reading a contact moved meanwhile. A row that stands and does not open refuses by name: a burn nobody can read never reads as unspent, and a carried value nobody can open never reads as absent. A floor composition reads no hosting row, so a locked hearth sorts no socket as a walker. `lares host`, `host roll` and `host invite` ride the custody door (`host.state` · `host.roll` · `host.invite`): a minted invite as a verb's outcome would rest in the daemon's document in the clear.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:342:* ''The gate's memory rows'' (specified in code; no gate calls them until the socket cutover): a sovereign gate's withdrawal memory rests one row per face key in the vessel's storage home, named by the face's proof-subject digest and sealed under the VK, so a locked vessel's disk names no face key (`gate-memory` in the carrier table; `packages/lararium-node/src/gate-memory-rows.ts`). Each write reads, decides and seals under one custody holder, and refuses where it would drop an event the row holds; a locked seat refuses by name. An older copy of a row restored by hand makes a gate forget until the next honest vessel dials, and no fence stands against that hand. A row that stands and does not fold whole refuses by name and reports it (`GateMemoryRowTorn`): the asking gate falls silent, no keep writes over the row, and a person repairs it by hand, where a row read as nothing would let a fresh memory admit a vessel the row once denied. No backup bundle carries the row: a vessel that stands again knows nothing (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof#/the-withdrawal-proof">>).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:343:* ''The session and the boot'': the daemon stands at the floor holding no VK and unlocks on a custody frame of its owner-only socket (`unlock` · `lock` · `custody` · `act` · `backup`, `packages/lararium-node/src/custody-frames.ts`), handled ahead of every verb, so the credential the CLI reads on its TTY reaches no receipt, outcome or log. One holder keeps the opened VK in node-main (`custody-holder.ts`); an unlock tears the standing composition down and stands a fresh one on the same floor (`open-node-vessel.ts`), a lock returns it to the floor, and three failed unlocks spend a boot's attempts. A composition that refuses above the floor leaves the floor standing and names its fault once. The settle sweeps a sidecar whose write never landed. The test door (`tools/unlock-test-custody.mjs`) opens marked scratch roots alone, and the marker earns one loud line in `vault status` and the boot log. Every boot composes at the floor: nothing stored lifts it. A daemon island holds no VK, so its archive exports cross the custody write door (`custody:write`) and the main thread seals them. Every broad sync port, the daemon island's and each wiki island's, crosses one hardened facade on both ends: an arrival that reads as no sync message drops at the port and never reaches a listener that would throw on it (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/island-repo.ts`). The daemon island's gates ask the main thread what a device's edge reads on its fleet's board through the dyad door (`dyad:ask`), which answers `aside` wherever it cannot read. Each fold of the fleet's edge board sets off the key side's settle on an unlocked vessel, with no timer and no person: the main thread places the island's `seat-duties` verb, awaits its answer and keeps the signed rolls (`packages/lararium-node/src/seat-settle.ts`; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae#/what-the-code-holds">>). Those two doors and the rest door answer the daemon island's channel alone: each worker's class binds at its spawn (`packages/lararium-node/src/worker-handle.ts`), a wiki island reaches the fetch door alone while its custody write and its rest ask refuse by name and its dyad ask draws `aside`, and a session island reaches no vessel door. A command that acts with no vessel standing opens its own key session at the first sealed row it touches (`packages/lares-cli/src/offline-custody.ts`): a terminal prompt, and under a marked scratch root the published test route. A sealed row's act rides an `act` frame of the custody door and never a store verb: one typed table bounds the acts (`packages/lararium-node/src/sealed-acts.ts`), a standing vessel answers with no second prompt, and beside a standing vessel a command opens no key session of its own, while a root's recovery split refuses there (`packages/lares-cli/src/sealed-act-door.ts`). The fleet mirror of a pet-name and a declared Handle rides that door too: `selves.carry` names a face and which name, the vessel's main thread reads the name off its sealed row and writes it onto that face's own persona plane and no other face's, only where that plane's rest seals (a clear rest refuses the carry and the name stays on its row), `lares persona sync` fills and never replaces, and no verb takes or answers a face's own name (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/waking-floor#/the-shape">>).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:361:* ''Thresholded admission and promotion'' stand built: the chartered classes derive from the charter's own seats and threshold (`chartered-classes.ts`); promotion approves the exact bytes' hash with purpose, surface, class and epoch (`promotion-approval.ts`, `lares nexus promote open|sign|check`); Kahu-cabal admission stands as its own act at the high-impact threshold, where a vouch admits nobody (`kahu-cabal-admission.ts`, `lares nexus cabal`) (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/kahu#/chartered-classes">>).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:370:* ''Noise IK, proof-first'': the gate emits nothing before a valid first message; the knock from `gateKnock` and `knockSegment` in `gate-bundle.ts` selects the sealed face gate, and Noise IK carries message one.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:375:* ''The admit signature the build owes'': the canon-document list and full sovereign sync `GateBundlePin` enter the signed bytes through the fleet answer and admit carriage; `device-admit.ts` mints the internal `device-admit/v1` edge. The browser's first proof rides `Sec-WebSocket-Protocol` (`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof`).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:376:* ''Owed (b), the knock tests offline'': the knock path computes an HMAC-derived segment (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/gate-bundle.ts`, `knockSegment`, `gateKnock`); an observer holding candidate keys tests a sniffed knock offline, so not echoing the key protects only against an observer with no candidates.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:385:* ''Working-layer law the build owes'': one working document per (face, wiki, slot kind); its address derives from a secret only that face's vessels hold. The working layer follows its wiki across recipe recomposition. A leaf with an admit and no seat writes nothing to face wikis until join completion. Vessel removal leaves the address standing; the gate and document membership refuse the removed vessel (operator ruling).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:405:* ''History at admission'' (operator ruling): sharing a bag's past with a newcomer must have stood declared when those edits got written. An inviter chooses between history the realm already marked shareable and a present-state admission, and never widens the audience for another writer's past. The design target keeps one logical bag name whose key rolls mark epochs: a removal rolls, a from-now admission rolls, and a with-its-past admission hands over the earlier epochs' keys.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:406:* ''Mutual removal'' (operator ruling; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae">>): both signed acts and both key branches stay, every member sees the conflict, and it ends in an explicit fork unless the realm's charter named a recovery council.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:409:* ''The rungs'': 0, an admitted crossing; 1, a carrier the node holds arrives and renders; 2, a typed field edit reaches the node and survives its restart, read from a fresh browser profile; 3, one human, many faces; 4, two hearths. Rungs 0–2 give the one-machine witness the working-Lararium ruling asks for, and the node's own read decides each rung, never a screenshot or a connected socket.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:450:* ''Integrity owed: face isolation, end to end'' (`K15` step 3, `B1`; `F6`'s slice three rides here with Wave B). Its witness: one adversarial multi-tab, multi-face run in a real browser, an unadmitted port, a stale generation, a cross-face sealed write and the last session's lock, where today only fake islands read them. MEASURED (the fresh read of Wave B; the readers, 2026-10-20). Wave B (PR #81) builds the guards and their reds on fake islands and the node; the real-browser adversarial run waits on Wave C's one SharedWorker per house.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:459:* `K15` One hive per face (#/rulings, 2026-10-18): each PersonaGroup owns its Keyhive identity, event store, registry, archive and content-key seat, and no identity stands above them. Build order, each step red-first: (0) before bytes move, the custody contract of <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero">>: the node and browser row census sorted D, F or S, the FCK key class, each face's own slot tree and recovery route, the carrier binding of face, row name and kind, and the overwrite contract generalized to a row-class key (#/rulings, a face's custody rows seal under its own key; a shared act never makes a shared secret) (the node census built, PR #70: each carrier row names its target classes, a LEAD mark and its open joint, and `encodeCarrierContext` spells the D and S seal context; the archive-row-selector joint traced and held open, PR #71: no archive site hands its row an authenticated PersonaGroup); (1) a substrate probe that two Keyhive instances in one process hold apart under interleaved acts, a reboot and a cross-read (measured: isolation holds, `packages/lararium-keyhive/tests/two-hives-one-process.probe.test.ts`), then a face context with its own store, registry, archive and key seat; (2) the face as the sole owner of its identity and group, the vessel's delegation gone from every face-bearing event (built, PR #68: `makeFaceBagDoor`, `faceOwnerVerifier`, a two-face event-byte capture its red, `W25`'s probe its regression), and 2b, a bag keeping one Document across boots (built, PR #68: `registerBagsDurably`, its record on the daemon doc for the vessel's ground and on each face's plane for that face's bags); the door grants the face's group before it records a Document (PR #69), so a crash between them re-enters to the same end; (2c, operator ruling 2026-10-19; built, PR #79) the atom cut: a random atom per (vessel, PersonaGroup) under that face's FCK signs every act on the face's behalf on node and browser, the place signer keeps the floor's duties alone, the wire subjects and verifiers move together, and its genesis, admit and founding-bootstrap deltas ride `X0` by `genesis/unbaked.json`, red-first on a thief holding the place seed deriving no veil and opening no group secret; on the local presence channel the session wears the mounted face, so a verb's presenter derives from the island's own atom and never from the CLI's unsigned `requestedBy`, the floor presents the place for floor acts alone, and a verb that names another face refuses by name (#/rulings, a session wears the face, 2026-10-11; a published atom key would link face and vessel on a wire); (3) sessions and registries routed by one face, no union, with `F6` slice three's asker-seals beside it, each sealer holding its row class's key (built, PR #81: the browser house keys by (PersonaGroup, persona root), the island proves each face through `gate:clear` while the holder holds no key, the island reads the fleet board's dyad itself, a fresh group mints a fresh atom, founding seeds key by their ask digest, and the node keys its atom and veil-archive rows by PersonaGroup digest; the daemon's last unions ride step 6); (4) content keys and removal per face, `K12`'s fresh group inside it; (5) a one-face restore and a herm that carries yet authors nothing; (6) the fence migration, identity bytes, split stores, slot trees and FCKs, and archive and custody formats together, under one identity model (#/rulings, sync carries, verification decides: the sealed anchor, the signed `@persona` log, verified projections): each D row (the atom's seed, its archive) seals under its face's FCK, where the node now seals them under the seated vessel key, and keys by its PersonaGroup, as the node's atom and veil-archive rows and the browser's atom row already do, where the browser's veil archive still keys by handle index. The isolation red: unlock face A alone, bypass every route, and try to open and replace B's occupied carriers with every key A holds, the VK included; each open fails, B's bytes stand unchanged, and A's bundle restored on a fresh vessel holds nothing of B. Lead: DreamNet-Wright after `W26`'s floor slice lands. K, W. Wave C (step 6 under the identity anchor, `readFace` as the one door with its census) landed in PR #86 on 2026-10-23. Wave D (the FCK fence, kit `docs/pono/k15-wave-d-lane`) and `K15-H` (the Handle owner rides the anchor, the row in `docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane`) build beside each other; `K17`'s realm leg (`docs/pono/k17-realm-lease-lane`) follows Wave D.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:460:* `B1` Browser custody. The custody API stands specified in `browser-custody.ts`: a passphrase or paper (2-of-3) slot binds the slot tree, the device seed and every Keyhive Archive move into sealed carriers through the mesh's one sealed writer, a wrong route refuses and changes no byte, a locked keystore refuses `sealed-locked` before any mint, and the clear-password act asks through the confirm door and answers only to a literal yes. The boot stands (PRs #48 and #61): the vessel lock gives back on a throw and a `sealed-locked` boot retries in the same page, the web boot asks the unlock through its own form, the clear verb answers `asks` and calls no door before a literal yes, the wiki's `tm-clear-password` road asks through TW5's confirm road and writes no synced tiddler, the question names what it clears, and a declined unlock retries in the page. Under #/rulings (a shared act never makes a shared secret) the browser holds no vessel key, so the clear names one face and clears that face's rows, built inside `K15` steps 0 through 3. Owed: the persona roots, which still rest in the clear outside the tree, sealed under it, with the mint refusing until a slot binds (#/rulings); the browser's vessel-key rotation; and the passkey slot, after its derivation gets measured (`B3`) and never alone. Each tab asks for its own unlock, and the ask admits that tab to its face's open hive while the holder keeps a face's keys only while some session of that face stands unlocked (#/rulings, 2026-10-18; the research and its leads at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/session-unlock-2026">>). Built with `K15` step 3 (PR #81): the holder answers a port only for a session it admitted, an unadmitted port asking for a sealed body refusing by name, and the last session of a face to close locks that face's hive; the production holder lifecycle stays a named skip on every engine until Wave C's one SharedWorker per house. B.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:468:* `K12` A fresh PersonaGroup for a seat no hand can revoke (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae#/keys">>). The PersonaGroup stands as a Keyhive group, so every other seat's revocation rolls the bags the group reaches (`persona-group-roll`); revoke authority follows the seating lineage, so a seat whose seating hand left, and the founder's own seat, leave only by a fresh group. Owed first: a name the face keeps across groups, since its plane names key on the group's id. It builds inside `K15`'s per-face removal step. K.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:470:* `H5` An invited user's root mints on her device, sealed; the herm carries a sealed copy. B.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:481:* `K17` The edge frontier (#/rulings, the edge frontier, 2026-10-20). Red-first: the frontier certificate and its verifier on node and browser alike; the signed empty genesis at every founding; registration of a raise into its signer's next frontier; the widening reader (admit, grant, a content-key seal) acting as of a qualifying frontier and waiting as unknown otherwise; the admit bundle carrying the frontier and its snapshot; the reader persisting its highest accepted head. Reds: a withheld first raise, a deleted local raise, a stale clean frontier, two conflicting frontiers, a missing snapshot, a concurrent raise and lower, an epoch rollover. Beside Wave C, on the spine. K.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:482:* `K18` The recovery door: guardian-quorum rotation of a persona root beneath its KEL prefix, then `reanchorAfterRotation`, then a re-admit carrying the current `@persona` log and signed frontier. Owed: no production door rotates a root today, and the ceremony waits on the guardian count, an open operator gate (`kahu#/seed-and-nexus`); `reanchorAfterRotation` stands proven as a library function (Wave C, <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane">> #/owed). K.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:483:* `K16` The Teshima Family Council (#/rulings, 2026-10-18; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm">>), `K15`'s acceptance story. Kalani founds a private council; Leilani joins it with two of her three faces. Red-first, after `K15`'s face context: (1) the council's hive as a Keyhive group holding no key of its own, its members the chosen faces' own identities; (2) an invite walks Leilani to the door, the threshold grafts each chosen face, a face leaves by its own act, and another's removal rides `kapae` or a fork by omission; (3) a member face's photo lands in its working layer of the council wiki and reaches the council's canon by `MOVE` (`W27`); (4) both chosen faces read it, the face kept back reads nothing and learns nothing, and no event in the council's history names a creator or issuer that ties two of Leilani's faces together; (5) a herm carries the sealed book and authors nothing (`K15` step 5). The e2e set stands four vessels: Kalani's, one per chosen face of Leilani's, and a herm. The e2e set walks the council at one hearth first: Kalani's seed charter holds the realm and Leilani's chosen faces walk there as guests, no Nexus founded (#/rulings, one charter). The two-hearth council follows, under the Nexus the two found, and there the member consult that lets a realm's documents cross between two operators reads a root map nothing fills (cabal-realm #/many-realms, owed), and the climb from seed charter to Nexus re-pins the realm by a named act (owed). Open joints: a quorum Handle with a seated key stands only where the council signs as one name, and that key signs collective acts alone, reaching no member's hive (#/the-steward-signer, owed). K, W.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:487:* `I1` The face intent plane (#/rulings, the channel of intent, 2026-10-20; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-intent-plane">>). Build order, each step red-first: `@intents-<tag>` minted by the PersonaGroup with its entry kinds (intent, outcome, asks and answer, claim, release and takeover, supersede and cancel), each signed by its device's atom and its id a content hash; stand-down and the three verb classes, with a single-effect verb addressed to "any device" refused at issue; the read-side winner; causal voids and the operator's release; the face-join summons moving off the daemon doc onto the plane, which closes two hearths of one face, beside the CLI naming its face per invocation; the daemon wiki's view pane; the rubric's witness (a hundred keystrokes and a save write no entry; one move writes one intent and one outcome); then the far agent's relay seat after its own research. Its reds stand at the carrier's #/the-reds. Its authority reads stand on the face's sealed identity anchor, so it builds after Wave C lands the anchor (operator, 2026-10-20, approving the controller's lean); the relay seat's own research wave follows it. Lead: a Sonnet Episkopos with a Sol and a Copilot seat. I.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:513:* `W15` A floor pin statement carries no causal position, and `hearthPinIndex` files first-wins, so a rotated floor key re-files only on restart (`admit-gate-pin.ts`, `place-floor-pin.ts`). W.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:515:* `W26` The system wikis release and every other wiki reads the floor (#/rulings, 2026-10-16). Slice 1 stands (PR #49): genesis carries the first floor, its manifest and the `lares` and `lararium` snapshots by CID, and `@oracle` reads that floor by CID. Slice 2 stands (PR #52): each vessel's system, crossroads and realm pointers rest in its own `@catalog`, and nothing writes the shared `@oracle` after genesis (`oracle-doc-no-writer.test.ts`). Slice 3 stands (lane `--w26-floor-3`): the founding lands the counted 1-of-1 Kahu admission for persona zero's group (`landFoundingAdmission`) and registers `lares` and `lararium` as realm bags of the hearth's realm under persona zero's per-Nexus key (`landKahuRealm`); `kahuCabalCanonAccess` has its production caller (`kahuReachSourceOf`); the keel mounts only what the realm names, the registered bag set and the `bags/` mirrors follow, and no catalog row names a system bag. Slice 6 stands: one predicate (`requireKahuReach`) guards the residency reactor, meme put and delete, draft placement and a realm steward's write, and the keyholder island's verifier carries it for `--in-wiki` verbs. Slice 4 stands: the release (`floor-release`: body, CID, steward seal by a seated Kahu key, the cabal's high-impact approval of the manifest's exact bytes, the charter's epoch lineage), the chain fold, `lares nexus release`, the porch (`GET /floor/<Nexus AID>`, `/cas/<cid>` for the head's blobs), the browser's verified read, and the flow map's own `flow-pointer` domain in place of the retired `oracle-pointer`. The build runs six slices in order, under the architecture of #/rulings (2026-10-18), its shape and evidence at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w26-floor-lane">>: (1) the floor manifest and its read-face, genesis baking the first floor; (2) each vessel's pointers leave the shared document for its bootstrap, re-cutting `W21`; (3) the Kahu realm holds the live system documents, and a one-seat founding lands its 1-of-1 Kahu admission; (4) the release answer on the crossroads, folding `P8`; (5) the accept act per (face, Nexus), which follows Wave C's face context since its accepted floor rests as a face's D row; (6) reach into system canon refuses every hand outside the cabal. OWED: a browser Kahu hand rides Wave C's face context (the browser composes no board reader and reads as a stranger, fail closed); a sibling device of a seat-holding face reads the floor until that context carries the charter and the board to it; the carriage `canon` names (`device-admit.ts` `admitCanonDocs`, the browser's `hearth-canon`) read rows nothing writes now, and retire with `W21`'s rest. W.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:521:* `P12` A realm's edge board and vouch board cross by a lane of their own, and a fleet's edge board by the sibling lane; both composers have yet to seat those lanes (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae#/four-edges">>). May follow.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:524:* `W28` The sealed channel's frame layout (`gate-exchange.ts` `GATE_FRAME`, tags `0x01` to `0x13`) still reads "provisional", owned by no row, while both operators' vessels speak it on every dial (`face-dial.ts`, `face-gate.ts`). It freezes before the bake: the tag table, the fragment bound and the verdict length, with a reserved-tag rule so a later frame adds a tag and moves none. Pairs with the `W10` research pair, since both move the dial's bytes once. W.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:574:* `K8` The face-proof gate reads the admitted key's hand-over line, as the socket gate does. The key and its line stand built: a face's per-Nexus key mints at random into its sealed row and re-issues by a hand-over the carriage board carries (`nexus-leaf.ts`, `lares persona reissue`; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof#/the-key-hierarchy">>). The remainder rides the socket cutover. W.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:576:* `K14` The restored face's provisional standing (#/rulings; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/custody#/the-restore">>). The mark, guardian or chair view, confirm verbs and three authority-changing refusals stand. Owed: provisional guards at the root-signed crossing, edge kapae, device admit, two-founder act and session signer's authority purpose; a sibling view needs independent proof; the guardians' recovery path where every party stays unreachable. K, W, N.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:582:* `P19` Cabal acts across a roll: an act counts only under the epoch it names, so after a seal roll standing reads `absent` until the seats re-admit at the new head; anchored ancestry, which `lares nexus members` reads, carries them, and an `onRolled` refold for the cabal verbs follows once a live reading folds them. It lands with `P20`, under the same writer rule. P.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:583:* `W10` The knock tests offline for an observer with candidate keys (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/gate-bundle.ts`, `knockSegment`, `gateKnock`): accepted as a named leak once IK lands. W, canon.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:587:* `W20` Burned names outside the wire's files still guarded by name: the CLI's unknown-command list, the keyhive cabal names, the browser's boot-invite-burned store (`browser-vessel-identity.ts`). W.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:588:* `W22` `composeCasTransits` in `node-cas.ts` shapes `P10`'s client leg and gets wired; `openBrowserVessel`'s `walkInvite` option stands without a caller, while the CLI's `walkInvite` runs `walk invite`. W.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:591:* `F1` The scoped document view stands specified in mesh (`session-document-view.ts` over `gated-sync-leg.ts`); the pool's surface door (`mountSurface`) and the island kernel's half ride it, and no production caller mounts a surface. Owed: every interactive surface mounts under it in place of the broad sync port, which waits on a verified face (train W) and on callers that hold a session (`F4`, `F6`); the share verdict's caller keeps an owner from offering a session island a document beyond its facets; an admitted leaf's relay adapter wears the one-way gate over its hearth's canon documents, and the hearth wears that gate's twin toward its leaves (`hearth-canon.ts`, `open-browser-vessel.ts`, `open-node-vessel.ts`); a wiki island's verbs that read the catalog document move to the view's catalog ask. O1.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:599:* `H7` One doctrine line still calls an introduction's lifetime unruled (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/membership-doctrine#/the-invite">>). H, canon.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:602:* `B5` The leaf continuity walk (`tools/browser-weld/leaf-continuity.mjs`) drives an offline founding, reload, and Binding Gate fault that must refuse; the admit and join path still lacks a real-browser proof. B.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:639:* Guardian count and threshold remain with the operator (#/open); bundles carry enrolled guardian sets and the restore checks them (#/rulings).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:663:* `W21` A joinee mounts the hearth's `@lararium` corpus read-only beside its own, while the oracle plane never crosses (#/rulings, 2026-10-16). Each vessel's pointers rest in its own `@catalog` (PR #52), so a joined vessel's pointer no longer replaces its hearth's, and `shared-oracle-doc.probe` holds that two synced vessels each keep their own. The rest rides `W26`'s floor slices: a joinee reads its hearth's floor by the release and its CIDs (slice 4), where slice 5's accept act moves its pin; a sibling device of a seat-holding face reads the floor until Wave C's face context carries the charter and the board to it, and `device-admit.ts` states the law. W.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:710:# ''Landed ahead'': `seal cofound open|join|seal` across two vaults; the two-vault admit, revoke, kapae and roll-anchor partials; rolls across both vaults as one carried circle, a third chair and a passed chair; the two-root import, boot and restart witness; the Offering act's scope, folded only inside its own Nexus.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:725:# ''Built'': fleet join on every face carries a device edge, face certificates, grants, a sealed address secret, the charter, the household admit and the floor pins; the admit and fleet answer sign the full sovereign sync route pin after N's cosign door.
