bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:759:# Canon: one pass on the invite doctrine.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:770:# ''Built'': guardian enrolment's typed event, command and sealed per-face row; bundles carry enrolled guardian sets and restore after enrolment; root cards rebuild the root through the checked restore; a fresh hearth restores its face as persona zero.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:781:# The automated witness: two vessels from one image digest, no volume in common, a courier that carries files alone; it proves two seeds, one AID on both sides, each founder held at the other's gate, an edit crossing both ways and reading back after each restart and unlock, a third root ADDED as a seat and contracted as a carrier, and a dormant node that wakes, imports the lineage and presents its admit.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:801:* ''The shadow at the gates.'' The law of removal's reach stands whole at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae#/reach">> (operator ruling): four marked edges, two hands, rolls that carry shadows, a ledger that keeps what a reader counted, a consult at every gate, and keys that never outrun standing. <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae#/what-the-code-holds">> names each part the code holds and each part that stays owed, and this carrier keeps no copy of that list. The cosign door's verdicts and envelope stand ready for train N's door to adopt. The sealed store's key roll subscribes to the seat's roll and lands with its own train.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:838:Nexuses rejoin through presented admits; every old admit names an old AID and reads dead by construction.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:847:# ''Guardians and recovery.'' The enrolment shape stands ruled (#/rulings). Guardian count and threshold at enrolment, request authentication, the veto, a person's death and succession, the catastrophe rite and any third key, and a Handle's DNS binding stand open at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/kahu#/seed-and-nexus">>.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:860:# ''Removal's reach.'' The model stands ruled (#/rulings; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae#/four-edges">>). Five questions stay the operator's, each with the house's lean. Whether an edge act may ever use the emergency class (lean: never). Whether a seated member under a member shadow keeps a seat's signature until the next roll (lean: yes, a seat leaves by a roll alone). What a recovery council holds after a mutual removal (lean: nothing built; the fork stands as the one exit). Whether a holder's key reads at its log's current head, so a recovered face keeps its edges (lean: yes, owed with the resolver of #/side-lanes). Whether a counted raise moves the keys while a lift still races it (lean: yes, remove-wins reaches the keys, and a lift then seats afresh). Two more came with the key side. What removes a seat no standing hand can revoke, the founding vessel's own among them (lean: a fresh group, at the re-founding that moves the PersonaGroup to a Keyhive group). Whether a vessel that holds no revoke authority goes on trying a raise until it sees the seat leave (lean: yes, and each try hands the roll on again, so the content key rolls whoever revokes the seat).
