bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:268:`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/membership-doctrine#/the-invite`. The decisions below constrain a slice
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:335:* ''The vessel-identity family'': the persona roster, the worn-face selector, the pet-name map, the declaration map and the published-face record rest sealed under the VK as hot rows; each persona root rests as a cold row, opened for one act; the floor vessel key rests beside its signed inception, every load proves that inception, and no next-key seed or commitment rides it. The roster commits a root: a mint writes the root row, then the roster line that carries the root's public key, so a reading of a public key answers off the hot roster and opens no root. A root row with no roster line reads as an orphan: no reader holds it, `lares persona list` names it, and the same mint run again adopts it. A roster line whose root row went missing, or names another key, refuses by name at the act that needs the seed, and nothing mints over it. A hot row with nothing at its path reads as holding nothing; a row that stands and does not open, or opens to another shape, refuses by name at every read and every write. A vessel key mints only inside a held custody, and lands with its inception under the custody's one claim: the key file commits the mint, so two acts never commit two keys, and a boot loads a key and never mints one. The floor reads no row of the family, so a carried-Nexus reading by persona (a seated chair, a kept consent) answers empty until the key arrives, and a sovereign composition reads the roster whole before it stands (`packages/lararium-node/src/node-vessel-identity.ts`). A floor composition reads no roster, so it shuts every fleet lane: it sorts every device as set aside, sets a proven sibling aside, and its fetch door reads no peer as fleet, the pinned join gate's key included (`packages/lararium-node/src/floor-fleet-lanes.ts`). It still folds the one fleet board its own device edge names in the clear, so the Binding Gate reads this vessel's own seat at every standing.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:337:* ''The walk records'': each hearth a vessel walks at keeps one HOT row sealed under the VK, named by a digest of that hearth's gate key (`packages/lararium-node/src/node-walk-store.ts`). A record holds bearer invites, the hearth's grant and one receipt per carried document (`{ cid: "blake3:<hex>", ref, key }`, whose `key` opens that document), so it counts as a secret row. The row rests in the storage home of the custody seat: the store takes no directory, so no caller files it beside a document store the vessel key never spans. Nothing at a hearth's path reads as no walk there; a row that stands and does not open, opens to another shape, or rests filed under another hearth's name refuses the read, the list and the update by name, and an update seals a whole record or nothing. Each change reads, decides and seals under one custody holder, so one invite leaves a wallet once. A floor composition reads no walk record and presents no walk; a fresh browser device stands at the floor under its `#floor=` card, and a joined face crosses under its root-signed pin. A key that locks under a live walk costs the walk one message, which it logs. `lares walk`, `walk take` and `walk invite` ride the custody door (`walk.state` · `walk.take` · `walk.invite`): a carried invite as a verb's argument, or an invite as a verb's outcome, would rest in the daemon's document in the clear.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:338:* ''The hosting rows'': a hearth's hosting state, each spend and its walkers' carriage rest as HOT rows sealed under the VK, in the storage home of the custody seat (`packages/lararium-node/src/hosting-store.ts`, `hosting-carry.ts`). The sealed writer writes a whole file and appends to none, so each spend lands as ONE row of its own, named by a digest of its nonce or marker: the row's presence IS the burn, and it reads, decides and seals under one custody holder. The spend row commits a redemption, and what rides ahead of it re-derives: the grant from the epoch, the leaf, the nonce and the claim, so a crash before the answer replays as `retry`; the operator's counts from the rows standing, by name. A roll's state row commits the roll, and the hosting doc re-derives from it: the next roll and each sovereign stand land an act the sealed state holds and the doc lacks (`landHostingActs`). The sweep of dead epochs' rows passes through the seat's removal door (`removeCustodyRow`), which removes only a row this vessel's key opens; a spend that sealed after a roll retired its epoch burns nothing live and leaves with the next sweep. Each carried value rests as one row whose name carries its address and its length, so a guest's bytes read off its rows and no counter stands beside them. One process serves a hearth's carriage (the standing vessel's own gate, under its store claim), and its contacts and deposits run in turn, so a quota reads the bytes the last deposit left and a reclaim never discards on a reading a contact moved meanwhile. A row that stands and does not open refuses by name: a burn nobody can read never reads as unspent, and a carried value nobody can open never reads as absent. A floor composition reads no hosting row, so a locked hearth sorts no socket as a walker. `lares host`, `host roll` and `host invite` ride the custody door (`host.state` · `host.roll` · `host.invite`): a minted invite as a verb's outcome would rest in the daemon's document in the clear.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:405:* ''History at admission'' (operator ruling): sharing a bag's past with a newcomer must have stood declared when those edits got written. An inviter chooses between history the realm already marked shareable and a present-state admission, and never widens the audience for another writer's past. The design target keeps one logical bag name whose key rolls mark epochs: a removal rolls, a from-now admission rolls, and a with-its-past admission hands over the earlier epochs' keys.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:459:* `K15` One hive per face (#/rulings, 2026-10-18): each PersonaGroup owns its Keyhive identity, event store, registry, archive and content-key seat, and no identity stands above them. Build order, each step red-first: (0) before bytes move, the custody contract of <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero">>: the node and browser row census sorted D, F or S, the FCK key class, each face's own slot tree and recovery route, the carrier binding of face, row name and kind, and the overwrite contract generalized to a row-class key (#/rulings, a face's custody rows seal under its own key; a shared act never makes a shared secret) (the node census built, PR #70: each carrier row names its target classes, a LEAD mark and its open joint, and `encodeCarrierContext` spells the D and S seal context; the archive-row-selector joint traced and held open, PR #71: no archive site hands its row an authenticated PersonaGroup); (1) a substrate probe that two Keyhive instances in one process hold apart under interleaved acts, a reboot and a cross-read (measured: isolation holds, `packages/lararium-keyhive/tests/two-hives-one-process.probe.test.ts`), then a face context with its own store, registry, archive and key seat; (2) the face as the sole owner of its identity and group, the vessel's delegation gone from every face-bearing event (built, PR #68: `makeFaceBagDoor`, `faceOwnerVerifier`, a two-face event-byte capture its red, `W25`'s probe its regression), and 2b, a bag keeping one Document across boots (built, PR #68: `registerBagsDurably`, its record on the daemon doc for the vessel's ground and on each face's plane for that face's bags); the door grants the face's group before it records a Document (PR #69), so a crash between them re-enters to the same end; (2c, operator ruling 2026-10-19; built, PR #79) the atom cut: a random atom per (vessel, PersonaGroup) under that face's FCK signs every act on the face's behalf on node and browser, the place signer keeps the floor's duties alone, the wire subjects and verifiers move together, and its genesis, admit and founding-bootstrap deltas ride `X0` by `genesis/unbaked.json`, red-first on a thief holding the place seed deriving no veil and opening no group secret; on the local presence channel the session wears the mounted face, so a verb's presenter derives from the island's own atom and never from the CLI's unsigned `requestedBy`, the floor presents the place for floor acts alone, and a verb that names another face refuses by name (#/rulings, a session wears the face, 2026-10-11; a published atom key would link face and vessel on a wire); (3) sessions and registries routed by one face, no union, with `F6` slice three's asker-seals beside it, each sealer holding its row class's key (built, PR #81: the browser house keys by (PersonaGroup, persona root), the island proves each face through `gate:clear` while the holder holds no key, the island reads the fleet board's dyad itself, a fresh group mints a fresh atom, founding seeds key by their ask digest, and the node keys its atom and veil-archive rows by PersonaGroup digest; the daemon's last unions ride step 6); (4) content keys and removal per face, `K12`'s fresh group inside it; (5) a one-face restore and a herm that carries yet authors nothing; (6) the fence migration, identity bytes, split stores, slot trees and FCKs, and archive and custody formats together, under one identity model (#/rulings, sync carries, verification decides: the sealed anchor, the signed `@persona` log, verified projections): each D row (the atom's seed, its archive) seals under its face's FCK, where the node now seals them under the seated vessel key, and keys by its PersonaGroup, as the node's atom and veil-archive rows and the browser's atom row already do, where the browser's veil archive still keys by handle index. The isolation red: unlock face A alone, bypass every route, and try to open and replace B's occupied carriers with every key A holds, the VK included; each open fails, B's bytes stand unchanged, and A's bundle restored on a fresh vessel holds nothing of B. Lead: DreamNet-Wright after `W26`'s floor slice lands. K, W. Wave C (step 6 under the identity anchor, `readFace` as the one door with its census) landed in PR #86 on 2026-10-23. Wave D (the FCK fence, kit `docs/pono/k15-wave-d-lane`) and `K15-H` (the Handle owner rides the anchor, the row in `docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane`) build beside each other; `K17`'s realm leg (`docs/pono/k17-realm-lease-lane`) follows Wave D.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:470:* `H5` An invited user's root mints on her device, sealed; the herm carries a sealed copy. B.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:483:* `K16` The Teshima Family Council (#/rulings, 2026-10-18; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm">>), `K15`'s acceptance story. Kalani founds a private council; Leilani joins it with two of her three faces. Red-first, after `K15`'s face context: (1) the council's hive as a Keyhive group holding no key of its own, its members the chosen faces' own identities; (2) an invite walks Leilani to the door, the threshold grafts each chosen face, a face leaves by its own act, and another's removal rides `kapae` or a fork by omission; (3) a member face's photo lands in its working layer of the council wiki and reaches the council's canon by `MOVE` (`W27`); (4) both chosen faces read it, the face kept back reads nothing and learns nothing, and no event in the council's history names a creator or issuer that ties two of Leilani's faces together; (5) a herm carries the sealed book and authors nothing (`K15` step 5). The e2e set stands four vessels: Kalani's, one per chosen face of Leilani's, and a herm. The e2e set walks the council at one hearth first: Kalani's seed charter holds the realm and Leilani's chosen faces walk there as guests, no Nexus founded (#/rulings, one charter). The two-hearth council follows, under the Nexus the two found, and there the member consult that lets a realm's documents cross between two operators reads a root map nothing fills (cabal-realm #/many-realms, owed), and the climb from seed charter to Nexus re-pins the realm by a named act (owed). Open joints: a quorum Handle with a seated key stands only where the council signs as one name, and that key signs collective acts alone, reaching no member's hive (#/the-steward-signer, owed). K, W.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:508:* ''Research pair: the knock's leak'' (`W10`, moved from after the seat: its answer moves the dial's bytes, so it lands before the bake or closes `W10` as an accepted leak). Its question: the IK path, or its equal, that lets a client prove itself first without breaking admission or pinning. Lenses: applied cryptography / operational migration risk.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:524:* `W28` The sealed channel's frame layout (`gate-exchange.ts` `GATE_FRAME`, tags `0x01` to `0x13`) still reads "provisional", owned by no row, while both operators' vessels speak it on every dial (`face-dial.ts`, `face-gate.ts`). It freezes before the bake: the tag table, the fragment bound and the verdict length, with a reserved-tag rule so a later frame adds a tag and moves none. Pairs with the `W10` research pair, since both move the dial's bytes once. W.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:536:* ''Integrity owed: the bake's cross-product'' (`X0`, touching `K15` step 6, `W26`, `G37`). Its witness: one matrix over the pre-bake and post-bake artifacts, every old CID refused after the bake and a fresh two-of-two founding standing, rather than greens read row by row.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:538:* ''Integrity owed: the habit flip at the bake'' (`X0`, `G37`). Before the bake the house runs re-genesis freely, since no CRDT document survives; after it, a re-genesis costs every CID a second operator pins. Its witness: a census of each instrument, fixture, brief and runbook line that assumes a free re-genesis, each named to flip or retire inside the bake's own commit, never after it.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:544:* `X0` The founding bake: one deliberate re-genesis before a second operator stands, after which CIDs are meant to last because another operator pins them. It moves together `K15` step 6 (identity bytes, split stores, slot trees and FCKs, archive and custody formats, each face's random device veil), the place KEL's pre-rotation and the scoped place signer (the signer frames each duty's domain itself, signing `len(D) ‖ D ‖ preimage` and its verifiers the same, so no signed floor image carries its own separation; until then each of the five floor duties binds its domain by an exact head matcher), `W26`'s closing bake (the floor release), and `G37`'s preimage and format renames (`engine/v1` and its kin, the floor announcement's kind, the genesis seed and CAS formats). Each member carries its own readiness red, so the bake waits on the slowest by name, never on a date; the bake's own red: a fresh genesis founds, no CID from before the bake verifies after it, and a mixed old archive refuses by name. The gate it opens: a second operator may found a Nexus fresh at two of two. X.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:583:* `W10` The knock tests offline for an observer with candidate keys (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/gate-bundle.ts`, `knockSegment`, `gateKnock`): accepted as a named leak once IK lands. W, canon.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:587:* `W20` Burned names outside the wire's files still guarded by name: the CLI's unknown-command list, the keyhive cabal names, the browser's boot-invite-burned store (`browser-vessel-identity.ts`). W.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:588:* `W22` `composeCasTransits` in `node-cas.ts` shapes `P10`'s client leg and gets wired; `openBrowserVessel`'s `walkInvite` option stands without a caller, while the CLI's `walkInvite` runs `walk invite`. W.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:599:* `H7` One doctrine line still calls an introduction's lifetime unruled (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/membership-doctrine#/the-invite">>). H, canon.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:604:* `X0b` The idempotent-by-intent pass, after the founding bake, paralleling the isomorphic-by-intent law (operator, 2026-10-19): a replay, a reboot and a retry land nothing new. Every row names itself by its content or its causal id, never a clock or a counter; every write reads first-writer-wins or merges by its CRDT; every boot reads as a function of its stores; and every multi-step act either completes or re-enters to the same end. Its instrument: N boots, each Archive replayed twice, each verb retried, and the second pass of each adds no head and no row. Each finding before the bake cures as its own bug; its instrument runs once before the bake as a census beside `G37`, so a finding that renames a persisted row lands inside the bake, and this pass sweeps what remains. X.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:631:* ''The bake's critical path in the operator's hands'' (`X0`). Once strides 1 to 3 stand built, these gate the ceremony and no lane can supply them: guardian count and threshold (`K18`, #/open); the domain and its two credential files (`A2`); one run on the real LAN (`A4`); the device measures (`B3`); the second machine and its operator for the fresh start (`X3`). The operator gathers them at their own pace; none blocks a lane today.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:759:# Canon: one pass on the invite doctrine.

